# K-Means Clusternig
We cant always rely on having training data sets to train our models. Sometimes we want to identify patterns in the data naturally. This is where K-Means Clustering comes in.
Its a type of model that looks for patterns or clusters in the data to find meaning. Given it does not use a training dataset to do this, it is known as an unsupervised model. 

# Background
The objective of clustering is to separate data into groups that are similar. To do this, we must define two things:

 - How many groups do we want to sort the data into?
 - How do we define how they are similar?
